===Etymology===
Bourbon, a county in US State of Kentucky.  The place name derives from a French royal family, from {{etyl|fr|en}} ''Bourbon l'Archambault'', chief town of a lordship in central France, from {{etyl|cel-gau|en}} [[w:Borvo|Borvo]], a local Celtic deity associated with hot springs, from {{etyl|cel-pro|en}} {{term/t|cel-pro|*borvo||froth, foam}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɜː(r)bən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[whiskey]] [[distill|distilled]] from a mixture of grains in which more than half is [[maize]], aged in [[oak]] [[barrel|barrels]]. Made chiefly in the United States.
# A serving of bourbon
# A [[Bourbon biscuit]]

